cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "powerenvelope: measured energy per useful decision on a duty-cycled on-board pipeline"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/powerenvelope"
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
abstract: >-
  Measures the factor by which energy per inference understates the energy per
  useful decision of a duty-cycled on-board autonomy pipeline, and decomposes
  that factor into the rejection factor, the duty-cycle factor and the
  nominal-versus-measured active-power error, with the residual reported. Energy
  is the trapezoidal integral of the INA3221 VDD_IN rail power over the whole
  run, sleep windows included; a useful decision is an inference that passes a
  declared confidence and geometry gate, counted from committed per-inference
  records. Includes an analytic duty-cycle model whose every component is
  measured, a measured rail-accounting ratio against load, a between-run
  interval from repeated reference runs, and a learned mean-active-power
  predictor restricted by specification to descriptors an operator could state
  without running the pipeline. Research-grade; not flight-qualified, not
  certified, and not approved for operational aerospace use.
keywords:
  - energy-per-decision
  - duty-cycle
  - ina3221
  - jetson-orin-nano
  - hardware-in-the-loop
  - edge-ai
